  "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nI’m using the docker image of Synapse (1.57.1). I thought about to upgrade to 1.60 via portainer with the latest image.\r\nI stopped my 1.57.1 container and started duplicating it. The duplicate fails with error message \"failure mount point /data\", so I switched back to my old container.\r\n\r\nOn my previous server I used synapse with a virtual env. The update process was done in a few seconds. The docker thing is really time consuming. Maybe this would be a good workaround for my use case?:\r\n\r\nI logged into the container and figured out, that synapse is installed via pip. Would a \r\n\r\n`pip install --upgrade matrix-synapse`\r\n\r\njust do the update?\r\n",
